{:name "note-conventions"
 :purpose "What a projector note is and where each part of it is edited, for anyone, owner or agent, who reads or writes a note in a projector vault. A convention: never fired by tick. Source: projector's docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, principles C1, C3, C4, C6, C8, C10 and C11, and the pj-about skill, where the note format is written down."
 :executor :either
 :procedure "A note is a markdown file in one of the vault's four places: notes/ (any depth), projects/<id>/ (README.md there is the project note <id>, AGENTS.md beside it is instructions, never a note), daily/ (notes carrying day) and inbox/ (intake's cards: being there is what unjudged means, so no file stores it). A .md anywhere else is a stray that pj check reports. Carrying a status is what makes a note work; a note without one is a thought and may just sit there. Status is lifecycle only: blocked, staleness, type, linked and kernel are computed axes, never stored (C11), and every count and badge is computed, never inferred by a model (C8). No facet is privileged (C4): which axis is the lifecycle, and which of its values mean open, met, missed or dropped, is the vault's to say in .projector/config.yaml (kernel.commitments and kernel.verdicts), never the app's or an agent's guess; a value in neither, such as planning or on-hold, is no commitment at all. C1: the markdown files are the source of truth; every index is derived and disposable. C3: notes stay agent-editable with plain file writes, no API and no app running; an agent that writes a note by hand respects the vocabulary in .projector/facets.yaml (a single-valued axis holds one value). C6: the body is free-form (description, links, files, images), no template; a body line starting `Done when` is the criterion the kernel shows for the note's intent. C10: structure is edited by gesture, content in the panel: facets, parent and edges by drag and bulk bar in the app; title, body, links and project: only in the note panel (?note=). In the kernel a note is the entity vault:<vault>:<id>, kind note. pj kernel import, run as the owner, reports each note on the commitments axis as a commitment keyed by that alias and each status change as a vault/status event keyed vault:<vault>:<id>:<status> (@n on a status held before); each note in the kernel.days folder is a vault/day event keyed vault:<vault>:day:<date>, never a commitment. A value kernel.verdicts maps, set in the app, is also the owner's observation through bin/kernel observe; the owner's answer in the kernel is written back into the note through the same map."
 :criterion "Every note that carries work carries a status and every thought carries none; no note stores what is derived (blocked, staleness, type, linked, kernel, intake); no edit introduces a body template; after pj kernel import, the kernel's intent about each note on the commitments axis is open, met, missed or dropped exactly as the vault's map reads its value, and a note whose value maps to nothing has no open intent."
 :trigger {:manual true}}
